# Bring the platen and shroud to a plateau
# Sets both zones to the temperature, turns their thermal control on and waits for the
# platen to read within 2 °C of it, from above or below, for at most the minutes given.
# The platen is the control temperature: GEVS starts a unit's plateau when it is within
# 2 °C (GSFC-STD-7000B, 2.6.3.2.3). Both zones stay on, holding the temperature, until
# a step turns them off. Below 30 °C it needs liquid nitrogen. Set how fast the zones
# move first, with hvc platen rate and hvc shroud rate.
block plateau at <temperature:number -150..120 C> within <minutes:number 1..600 min>
load rLACO

hvc platen {temperature}
hvc shroud {temperature}
hvc platen on
hvc shroud on
until platenT >= {temperature-2} C within {minutes} min
until platenT <= {temperature+2} C within {minutes} min
